metal_hardware.rs opens the HardwareMetal port: the Vulkan raster's
whole shader rack (shade/vert/frag both variants, transfer, depth,
upright both variants) goes through the same GLSL sources into naga's
msl-out, and a real Metal device compiles all eight MSL libraries
(8/8, 23ms of translation, 1.6s of cold library build incl. shader
validation). compile_msl_stage generalizes the M0.5 vertex helper to
any stage + defines (WRITES_DEPTH, TO_IMAGE variants translate from
the same sources).

prepare() normalizes the three naga-front gaps in the Vulkan-GLSL
dialect, none touching meaning: sampler2D pairs split to Vulkan-GLSL's
separate texture2D+sampler (their texture() calls built back through
the sampler2D(t,s) constructor, samplers bound 10+), constant_id spec
constants flatten to plain constants (Metal pipelines configure via
defines), push_constant blocks become binding-24 uniform buffers (A2
binds a batch's words there), writeonly storage buffers drop the
qualifier (naga's IR can't carry store-only; Metal binds read-write),
and the precise qualifier naga lacks goes away.
